## STANDING LINES
- **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** (above and Step 0b). Re-read main and the head first; do not redo work already done: say which, with file and line.
- No message to any human. No comment on any pull request and no edit of it. **No Jira write.** Never delete (quarantine). No deploy, no `az`, no hosted site or database, no image push. No customer-readable word added to any file (you add none: you edit no file). No HPSM-POC anything. No HP tool integration (this lane builds none).
- **Closed lists** (paths, hashes, check names) are stated by their PROPERTY first and then "at least these"; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP.
- `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP; a check whose control does not fire is a fault in the check; never skip a failing step; a landed-looking green on a different tree than the merged one is not a pass (treeproof).
- **Commit rules:** one commit (the merge), the message frozen in Step 3, no ticket key, brief number, card id or person's name in it or in any text you write for Tuesday's use on the pull request. Record gitleaks at the commit (`scripts/secret-scan.sh --tree` and the range scan; the pre-commit hook does not run on a merge commit made by `git merge`: say so, and prove the scan by its own run). ONE plain push of ONE ref (never `--force`, never `+`); the ref moves by fast-forward only.
- **Git identity is never overridden.** The repo's own configured identity only, as the IDENTITY slot establishes it; never `git -c user.name/user.email`, never `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*`. READY prints `git log --format='%h %ae | %ce'` for every new commit (one), each email equal to the configured one.
- **Landing rule (quote, with its source):** `1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md:1799`, C-101 (1): "[the coordinator] squash-merges PR #88 pinned to head 2da99cab after re-reading CodeQL and the checks". The project's `CLAUDE.md` has no rule on merging or branches. **You push your branch only. Tuesday marks the pull request ready, applies the body text, reads CodeQL and lands it (head-pinned squash), and only after the independent review; none of that is yours.** A squash puts only the head's tree on main, so the merge commit is history on the branch only.
- **Records write rule** (HANDOVER paragraph above): build, encode, temp file, `os.replace`; never encode a whole file as ASCII when it already holds non-ASCII bytes (encode the ADDED bytes and check them).

